{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When YHWH your Elohim cuts off the nations, etc. Three cities you shall set apart for yourself</b>: This too is an explicit commandment, for He had already commanded concerning it (Exodus 21:13). But now He added to explain its laws, for He said, \"and you shall possess them and dwell in their cities and in their houses\" — to teach that they were not obligated in it except after possession and settlement, and so Joshua did. And He added, \"you shall prepare the road for yourself\" — that they be marked routes leading into them, and that one write \"refuge, refuge\" at the fork of the roads. And He added, \"and you shall divide the border of your land into three parts.\" And He further added to teach us the matter of unwitting intent, as He said (Deuteronomy 19:5), \"and one who goes with his fellow into the forest,\" etc. — and there are many midrashim that our Sages expounded in the pericope:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Ramban quotes the phrase וְשִׁלַּשְׁתָּ אֶת גְּבוּל אַרְצְךָ from Deuteronomy 19:3; the plain sense is 'you shall triple the border of your land,' i.e., divide it into three parts."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:39.058043641Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}